{
  "dom_id": "step-18871",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Splitting a Rational Expression With Two Terms in the Numerator",
  "problem": "Given that $\\dfrac{6y − 1}{3} = ay + b,$  what are the values of $a$ and $b?$",
  "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{6y − 1}{3} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac{6y}{3} - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac{6}{3} \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\\t\n\t\t2 \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\\t\t\n\t\t2y - \\dfrac 1 3 &.\n\t}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $ay+b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{(2)}_{⏟}}_{a}y+{{(-\\frac{1}{3})}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and $b=-\\dfrac{1}{3}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
